id: pm-rust-y12t
title: Digest hex formatting blocked the sha2 0.11 upgrade across every platform
description: "Formatting the Sha256 digest with the LowerHex shorthand tied document hashing to the GenericArray type that sha2 0.10 returns. sha2 0.11 returns a hybrid-array Array which does not implement LowerHex, so the dependabot upgrade failed to compile on ubuntu, macos and windows."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[3]: dependencies,hashing,release-gate
created_at: "2026-08-10T05:45:39.847Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-10T05:45:39.847Z"
deadline: "2026-08-17T00:00:00.000Z"
assignee: claude
author: claude
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: cargo test passes with sha2 pinned to 0.11.0 and the create contract golden hash 6eb97257a863250fafbcc2d460f0b9a08a1b864bebf2c725632258e3f72db01c is unchanged
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-rust-u4al,related,"2026-08-10T05:45:39.847Z",claude,"cli:create:dep",asserted
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T05:45:39.847Z",claude,Verified by pinning sha2 to 0.11.0 locally and running the full suite before committing the bump
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T05:45:39.847Z",claude,The golden hash in tests create_contract.rs is what makes this upgrade safe to prove rather than assume
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T05:45:39.847Z",claude,A formatting shorthand can be a hidden dependency on a transitive type. The LowerHex implementation belonged to generic-array rather than to sha2 so nothing in the call site named the crate that made it compile
